course: dictionary
lesson: 10347
title: Translate: words, meaning and shapes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To translate means to change words from one language into another, so that someone who does not speak the first language can understand. «Beowulf» is an Old English poem, so today it has to be translated before most people can read it.
explain: Translate can also mean to change something into a different form. «Translate a plan into action» means turning an idea on paper into something you actually do. The word into is your clue: something moves from one form into another.
explain: In maths, to translate a shape means to slide it to a new place without turning or flipping it. «Translate the triangle 3 squares right and 2 up» tells you the triangle moves, but it keeps its size, its shape and its direction.
fact: To translate means to change words from one language into another.
fact: «Translate from … into …» is a common phrase, such as translate from Latin into English.
fact: In Baghdad's House of Wisdom, scholars translated Greek, Persian and Indian books into Arabic.
fact: Reformers translated the Bible from Latin into German, English and other languages so ordinary people could read it themselves.
fact: In maths, a translation slides a shape to a new position without turning or flipping it.
exercise: «Reformers translated the Bible from Latin into German, English and other languages.» What does translated mean here? | Read it aloud very slowly | *Changed the words into other languages | Burned the books | Made copies of it in Latin only
exercise: «Translate the triangle 3 squares right and 2 up.» In maths, what happens to the triangle? | It turns around | It is flipped over like a mirror | It gets bigger | *It slides to a new place, without turning or flipping
exercise: Aisha says «translate a plan into action» means drawing the plan in a different colour. What does it really mean? | *To change the plan into something you actually do | To copy the plan exactly | To write the plan in another language | To lose the plan
test: «In Baghdad's House of Wisdom, scholars translated Greek books into Arabic.» Which language were the books changed into? | Latin | Greek | Persian | *Arabic
test: A friend says, «Translate the game into every language so everyone can play it.» What is the friend asking you to do? | *Change the game's words into each language so everyone can play | Lose the game's rules | Make the game harder to play | Play the game in only one language
exam: Which sentence uses translate to mean sliding a shape? | Translate the plan into action | *Translate the square 4 squares left | Translate the message from German into English | Translate the poem into Arabic
